# =====================================================================
# Aari Transactions · path-reorg cutover rules  (INERT — not yet active)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify ONLY reads a file named "_redirects". This file is ".ready",
# so it does NOTHING until you rename it. That keeps the live site safe
# while the cutover is staged.
#
# TO ACTIVATE (only after the new URLs test clean):
#   rename  _redirects.ready  ->  _redirects   then deploy.
# TO REVERT:
#   delete the line (or rename back to _redirects.ready) and deploy.
#
# The "301!" forces the redirect even though the old root file still
# exists, so originals stay in place as a backup. One line = one path.
# These three rules auto-handle every inbound link in aari-header.js,
# login-modal.js, aari-banner.js, aari-crm.html, prospecting.html, and
# broker-weekly-report.html — no need to edit those files.
# =====================================================================

# --- /tc-portal cockpits (lowest traffic — cut over first) ---
/eileen.html          /tc-portal/eileen.html      301!
/milennys.html        /tc-portal/milennys.html    301!
/broker-cockpit.html  /tc-portal/marlenyi.html    301!

# --- /portal (add after /tc-portal is confirmed live) ---
# /portal.html        /portal/portal.html         301!
# /tc-submit.html     /portal/tc-submit.html      301!

# --- /public auth pages (add after the above are confirmed) ---
# /register.html      /public/register.html       301!
# /login.html         /public/login.html          301!
